  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 114 PM CDT Sat Aug 15 2026\n\nShowers and isolated thunderstorms continue to nudge into east \ncentral SD this afternoon, though the activity has mainly stayed \nsouth of Hwy 212. This is all associated with a shortwave and \nelongated sfc trough along the MN/SD border. Humid but generally dry \nconditions are expected behind this trough as sfc high pressure \nbuilds in from the northwest tonight. Lighter winds and latent \nmoisture will likely lead to fog redeveloping tonight into Sunday \nmorning across the area. \n\nWhen the high exits Sunday night, additional shortwaves and a weak \nllj may gin up some showers, but more widespread precipitation \nchances are not anticipated until a cold front moves through Monday \nnight and Tuesday. There is a marginal risk (1 out of 5) for severe \nstorms Monday night with the front, and that risk will probably \nextend into Tuesday though location is still tenuous. While any sfc \nfocus shifts south, shortwave activity will increase across South \nDakota on Tuesday. At a minimum, this additional energy will bring \nincreased chances for locally heavy rain. The active and wet pattern \nfinally seems to wane in the latter half of the upcoming week.",
